[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T11:25:45-08:00","id":1183644,"title":"","content":"What do you think about crinos form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T14:39:18-08:00","id":1183712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1183644#post1183644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think about crinos form?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it looks great. Initially, I saw the pics on my phone and questioned the size of the Crinos form compared to the other pics, but they said it WILL be to scale. The pics were not. Just concept art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T16:56:31-08:00","id":1183763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1183639#post1183639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was announced shortly after the initial game announcement.<br /> <br /> I'm fine with this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I'd have a problem with fewer than these three forms, but glabro and hispo are relatively expendable if the publishers don't have the budget for all 5 forms. Also it looks like the concept art uses the glyphs for &quot;wolf,&quot; &quot;human,&quot; and &quot;werewolf,&quot; and maybe they didn't want to make up entirely new glyphs for &quot;glabro&quot; and &quot;hispo.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T23:05:53-08:00","id":1183841,"title":"","content":"I've missed the info about three forms and that was suprising. I think that crinos is bit too thin but it could be a matter of scale of picture. Still waiting for trailer or gameplay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T01:21:33-08:00","id":1183857,"title":"","content":"Would gladly see both Glabro &amp; Hispo go in exchange for mix-morphing. Yet, couldn't imagine how they might get this to work in a game either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent-lax3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfl1/v/t1.0-9/11999058_1477906402511404_6367649438608181692_n.jpg?oh=70d49fe91b2932b397dc24c5df2764ba&amp;oe=56A3338B\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","name":"Wolf-Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T02:38:26-08:00","id":1183865,"title":"","content":"Technologically mix-morph on a limited level wouldn't be that hard. Treat the body like a basic RPG character with legs, hands, torso, and head as places with equipment. You get a default filled in load out depending on your form, and some extra &quot;equipment&quot; that you can drop in (ex: claws on a human arm instead on a full lupine leg). Any time you try to alter the load out to something other than default, you make a skill check of some sort that's difficulty is based on the level of changed involved (both number of parts and each part would have a rating of some sort. Don't make it too easy, and have failing the check be bad to avoid people spamming it; on top of whatever penalties you'd naturally incur.<br /> <br /> It isn't going to ever be as flexible as what you can do in the books, but it's a functional framework if you wanted it in a game.<br /> <br /> I have no idea how to do it with the game they're building of course, because I have no idea what that's going to look like.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T02:51:03-08:00","id":1183867,"title":"","content":"The question is what sort of graphic engine they licensed. It might be hard to implement Glabro and Hispo forms in some of that... Although I would gladly see all forms, esspecialysince Hispo is my favorite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23823-radoslavus","name":"Radoslavus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T08:14:21-08:00","id":1183939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1183712#post1183712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it looks great. Initially, I saw the pics on my phone and questioned the size of the Crinos form compared to the other pics, but they said it WILL be to scale. The pics were not. Just concept art.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I do like how otherworldly it looks,though I am afraid it looks too slim, I suspect the creators will try to give the lean and agile aspect of the wolf side of crinos and make it look more brutaly feral than just brutal. I also love the fur colours, but probably the crinos head might better be a bit larger to give emphasis on bite maneuvers. He will also look awesome in the umbra.<br /> <br /> I also suspect that the creators will troll us, you will not be able to take glabro or hispo but you will see npcs in glabro or hispo with a mental '' you can't do it, nya nya nya nya nya'' in your brain.<br /> With quotings like Becket's wolf form, '' with training you will be able to do it one day''.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 02-09-2018, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T14:42:11-08:00","id":1184088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Radoslavus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1183867#post1183867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question is what sort of graphic engine they licensed.</div> </div> </div> </div>This baffles me. You don't need some sort of super special graphics engine for this. Diablo 2's graphics engine could handle this over 17 years ago when the expansion pack put a shapeshifter class in. The game had two forms you could shapeshift into, and multiple companion animals you could summon (including a regular wolf, and a dire wolf...). A &quot;change sprite&quot; combined with, &quot;altered stats,&quot; is not difficult graphics tech.<br /> <br /> Making the shapeshifting look good is a bit harder, but video gamers would hate it if transformations took significant time. A cool well rendered transformation in a cut scene is good. Having to wait 5 seconds every time you shift to watch the same animation is not. So shifting is probably going to be pretty straightforward graphically so it happens very quickly and players don't get annoyed waiting on the animations.<br /> <br /> I have to imagine that the only hurdle for including all five forms, is making them all useful in the intended game-play. Hispo is awesome, but I can easily foresee the issues for video game designers in trying to make it fun to use when Crinos and Lupus are already options. Video games tend to simplify RPG mechanics, which means the very subtle differences on when Hispo is more useful than Crinos or Lupus are easily lost in that. The technology to include Hispo might not be a problem, but it's still work to include it. A lot of work if the graphics are intensive enough. Putting in the relatively large amount of work needed to get Glabro and Hispo in the game when nobody is really going to use them because they're superfluous to gameplay is a giant waste of resources.<br /> <br /> So there's two options: Find a place for Glabro and Hispo in the game to justify putting them in (a decent amount of development work that still might not pay off), or cut them as game-play options and hope that the WtA fans understand the decision (hopefully not doing what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12906_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12906\" data-vbnamecard=\"12906\">Story Letter</a> just pointed out with them in the hands of NPCs).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T02:36:54-08:00","id":1184307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1184088#post1184088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This baffles me. You don't need some sort of super special graphics engine for this. Diablo 2's graphics engine could handle this over 17 years ago when the expansion pack put a shapeshifter class in. The game had two forms you could shapeshift into, and multiple companion animals you could summon (including a regular wolf, and a dire wolf...). A &quot;change sprite&quot; combined with, &quot;altered stats,&quot; is not difficult graphics tech.<br /> <br /> Making the shapeshifting look good is a bit harder, but video gamers would hate it if transformations took significant time. A cool well rendered transformation in a cut scene is good. Having to wait 5 seconds every time you shift to watch the same animation is not. So shifting is probably going to be pretty straightforward graphically so it happens very quickly and players don't get annoyed waiting on the animations.<br /> <br /> I have to imagine that the only hurdle for including all five forms, is making them all useful in the intended game-play. Hispo is awesome, but I can easily foresee the issues for video game designers in trying to make it fun to use when Crinos and Lupus are already options. Video games tend to simplify RPG mechanics, which means the very subtle differences on when Hispo is more useful than Crinos or Lupus are easily lost in that. The technology to include Hispo might not be a problem, but it's still work to include it. A lot of work if the graphics are intensive enough. Putting in the relatively large amount of work needed to get Glabro and Hispo in the game when nobody is really going to use them because they're superfluous to gameplay is a giant waste of resources.<br /> <br /> So there's two options: Find a place for Glabro and Hispo in the game to justify putting them in (a decent amount of development work that still might not pay off), or cut them as game-play options and hope that the WtA fans understand the decision (hopefully not doing what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12906_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12906\" data-vbnamecard=\"12906\">Story Letter</a> just pointed out with them in the hands of NPCs).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, Hispo is the preferred stalking/fighting form provding you don't mind dropping your gun or Glaive. <br /> <br /> \u200bI still think Glabro is accident that has in the very least some theatrical appeal to it. It's been used in a lot of old WW films. Before they could the perfect make-up and effects enough to add a descent snout and digit-graded feet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent-lax3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfl1/v/t1.0-9/11999058_1477906402511404_6367649438608181692_n.jpg?oh=70d49fe91b2932b397dc24c5df2764ba&amp;oe=56A3338B\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","name":"Wolf-Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T03:33:41-08:00","id":1184316,"title":"","content":"It still comes down to the difficulty in designing scenarios in a video game where it's going to matter of Hispo over Crinos enough you're going to feel it in play. <br /> <br /> For Glabro, the 'accident' mode of taking the form is just annoying as a game-play feature. It comes down to, &quot;you're stuck in Glabro for this part of the mission,&quot; which is a crappy handicap to make things more difficult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T11:54:27-08:00","id":1184468,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">However, I have been having this idea for awhile that there should be no predetermined Werewolf form for Garou aside from their own breed ones. Making them entirely mixed morphed, meaning that they could </span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">just change what they really need to with another roll of the dice. In </span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">fact, </span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">it would be harder to mix morph </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">certain traits depending on breed. </span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bNot really sure about Metis either. </span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Th