.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1186501#post1186501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Howler, I say, Howler blood!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That would make sense.....so many people love that &quot;last howler&quot; arch or the rebirth of the howlers. (I always liked the Croatan more)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T18:31:42-08:00","id":1186506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1186502#post1186502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That would make sense.....so many people love that &quot;last howler&quot; arch or the rebirth of the howlers. (I always liked the Croatan more)</div> </div> </div> </div>That would also explain why Fianna out of all the tribes was chosen, because they offer the best route to the whole 'corrupted bloodline' story. My guess is that Cahal's (the main character) son has gotten some nasty ancestors and is about to Dance the spiral. Or is foretold by the Dancers to be special somehow.<br /> <br /> I mean, Fianna legit falling would be a surprise, but I think it is the Howlers more likely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T18:49:41-08:00","id":1186512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1186192#post1186192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Something interesting to contemplate in the way of Red Talons and this conversation is that pale skin is an extremely recent development in humanity; Europeans didn't start turning pale until well after the last ice age was over (as in, around six millennia after it was over, give or take a few centuries). So, theoretically, Red Talons, who have conceptually resembled some form of &quot;older&quot; humanity, would likely not have Homid forms that pass for white.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah there are definitely human phenotypes that existed within the last ten thousand years that would look strange and out of place today. For example, Europeans native hunter gathers prior to the agricultural revolution had dark skin and blue eyes.<br /> <br /> There are also lots of peoples, whom while they still exist, once lived in very different places. For example a lot of blonde and red haired tribes populated central Asia and even western China and Mongolia. Most of those peoples migrated to the west over the millenia and the remnants were then pushed out by the Turkic expansion or destroyed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T20:51:51-08:00","id":1186532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1186501#post1186501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Howler, I say, Howler blood!</div> </div> </div> </div>Heart of Gaia 2: The Legend of Curly's Gold","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T23:23:19-08:00","id":1186552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1186502#post1186502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That would make sense.....so many people love that &quot;last howler&quot; arch or the rebirth of the howlers. (I always liked the Croatan more)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think that's because the Croatan don't have a readily available option to return them. BSDs have had since the very start &quot;White Howler throwbacks' as a really obvious plot hook.<br /> <br /> That being said I'd love to see Return of the Croatan plot..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T03:42:22-08:00","id":1186605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1186552#post1186552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I think that's because the Croatan don't have a readily available option to return them. BSDs have had since the very start &amp;quot;White Howler throwbacks' as a really obvious plot hook.<br /> <br /> That being said I'd love to see Return of the Croatan plot..</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that could be it, I always assumed it was the desire to be the angstiest angst muffin around","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T06:47:41-08:00","id":1186643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1186605#post1186605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess that could be it, I always assumed it was the desire to be the angstiest angst muffin around</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I LOVE the new Howlers in the tribebook, but that is because actual research and rethinking of the tribe was done there. In modern day games, Howler blood is kinda..ehh. Especially given how mixed BSDs are. It is like saying that having Genghish Khan as your distant ancestor makes you mongolian. Lion jumped ship, so did his tribe, BSD blood is still BSD blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T15:14:26-08:00","id":1186840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1186605#post1186605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess that could be it, I always assumed it was the desire to be the angstiest angst muffin around</div> </div> </div> </div>Heart of Gaia would have included it, the Outcasts book talks about &quot;Ronin BSD&quot; who have strong white howler blood. Purebreed even discusses the occasional white howler throw back among the BSDs.. The narrative is just easily there. a BSD who doesn't walk the spiral can start the whole &quot;return of the white howlers&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> There's however no Croatan to work from. Even the Croatan who didn't show up for the fight are covered. They are super dead. Their lineages at best taken by Wendigo and Uktena.. and possibly by some enterprising new comers. Having Croatan blood means little now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1186643#post1186643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, I LOVE the new Howlers in the tribebook, but that is because actual research and rethinking of the tribe was done there. In modern day games, Howler blood is kinda..ehh. Especially given how mixed BSDs are. It is like saying that having Genghish Khan as your distant ancestor makes you mongolian. Lion jumped ship, so did his tribe, BSD blood is still BSD blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>what makes a BSD is ..dancing the spiral. Someone of their blood who escapes is a thing. BSDs with pure breed 5 appear as white howlers at least in previous editions since its not covered in w20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T18:08:53-08:00","id":1186885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1186840#post1186840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heart of Gaia would have included it, the Outcasts book talks about &quot;Ronin BSD&quot; who have strong white howler blood. Purebreed even discusses the occasional white howler throw back among the BSDs.. The narrative is just easily there. a BSD who doesn't walk the spiral can start the whole &quot;return of the white howlers&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> There's however no Croatan to work from. Even the Croatan who didn't show up for the fight are covered. They are super dead. Their lineages at best taken by Wendigo and Uktena.. and possibly by some enterprising new comers. Having Croatan blood means little now.</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrugs* sure there's white howler throw backs are mentioned, but the books have made it rather clear that it doesn't really mean anything aside from Spirals wanting to hunt you. Toss in that now Pure Breed seems to be tied more to your tribe and being a spiritual rather then genetic concept....really a Howler throwback doesn't mean anything as Lion's out of the tribal sponsoring game. All three tribes have basically the same to go off of. Sure Lion's at least sponsoring packs (to which the Mokole book states Turtle's still sponsoring Mokole), but as far as the Howlers are concerned....they're done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T19:33:59-08:00","id":1186908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1186885#post1186885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *shrugs* sure there's white howler throw backs are mentioned, but the books have made it rather clear that it doesn't really mean anything aside from Spirals wanting to hunt you. Toss in that now Pure Breed seems to be tied more to your tribe and being a spiritual rather then genetic concept....really a Howler throwback doesn't mean anything as Lion's out of the tribal sponsoring game. All three tribes have basically the same to go off of. Sure Lion's at least sponsoring packs (to which the Mokole book states Turtle's still sponsoring Mokole), but as far as the Howlers are concerned....they're done.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm just saying why people focus on &quot;The return of the White Howlers&quot; or &quot;White Howler blood&quot; vs Croatan. I can see why people also ignore it. I'm just giving you reasons why people would focus on it. I mean &quot;Bob has White howler blood the BSDs are going to try to push his corruption!&quot; is a thing.. &quot;Bob has Croatan blood.. it means um... I don't know?&quot;<br /> <br /> Is Mokole Turtle the same as Croatan Turtle? I mean For example we explicitly know Africa Lion is not White Howler Lion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T19:37:45-08:00","id":1186909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1186908#post1186908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm just saying why people focus on &quot;The return of the White Howlers&quot; or &quot;White Howler blood&quot; vs Croatan. I can see why people also ignore it. I'm just giving you reasons why people would focus on it. I mean &quot;Bob has White howler blood the BSDs are going to try to push his corruption!&quot; is a thing.. &quot;Bob has Croatan blood.. it means um... I don't know?&quot;<br /> <br /> Is Mokole Turtle the same as Croatan Turtle? I mean For example we explicitly know Africa Lion is not White Howler Lion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mokole Turtle is intended to be the same one that the Croatan followed. It states the Croatan and Mokole got along through this common totem and that all Turtle did was withdraw from the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T00:45:11-08:00","id":1186973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1186840#post1186840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what makes a BSD is ..dancing the spiral. Someone of their blood who escapes is a thing. BSDs with pure breed 5 appear as white howlers at least in previous editions since its not covered in w20.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they still carry the genetic material for the generations before them, which includes inbreeding, exposure to toxic waste, exposure to whoknowswhat and Wyrmy taint. Even if they escape and get chosen, they still have to deal with all the messes their bloodline brings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T10:28:04-08:00","id":1187071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.gamereactor.se/nyheter/579273/Werewolf+Earth+Blood+Intervju+med+studion/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.gamereactor.se/media/26/_1982673_1600x900.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.gamereactor.se/nyheter/579273/Werewolf+Earth+Blood+Intervju+med+studion/\" target=\"_blank\"> Werewolf: Earth Blood - Intervju med studion - Gamereactor Sverige </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.gamereactor.se/nyheter/579273/Werewolf+Earth+Blood+Intervju+med+studion/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.gamereactor.se/nyheter/579273/Werewolf+Earth+Blood+Intervju+med+studion/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Huvudf&ouml;rfattaren f&ouml;r White Wolf, Martin Ericsson, samt \"game director\" Julien Desourteaux haffades av Gamereactors mycket flitiga TV-team i Paris f&ouml;r att prata lite mer om kommande Werewolf: Earth Blood. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T11:42:27-08:00","id":1187094,"title":"","content":"Hopefully it being called 'Werewolf: Earth Blood' is just wonky translation work, because that just sounds uninspiring and stiff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T03:13:24-08:00","id":1187257,"title":"","content":"The blood if the earth is lava, not peteroil, just saying ....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T08:31:00-08:00","id":1187293,"title":"","content":"<ul><li>The <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Tribe_(WTA)\" target=\"_blank\">thirteen tribes of the Garou</a> are contemplating going into war with humanity due to their greed and destruction of the planet.</li> <li>You do not choose your tribe at the start of the game.</li> <li>You do not control a party of characters, you are solitary. You have allies outside of combat however.</li> <li>Takes place in Nevada, Alaska and the redwood forests of Washington.</li> <li>You do not align yourself to tribes as you play through the game, but you will encounter them and learn about their perspective of the conflict with humanity and the Wyrm.</li> <li>Levels are semi-open and linear, but offers multiple ways to solve it similar to Deus Ex.</li> <li>Each region have a large hub with free-roaming environment and different activities to do. Aid spirits of nature, such as destroying a dam to earn the favor of a river spirit, or destroy outposts. One such favor to a spirit can for example open a shortcut between regions or grant more side-missions. The hub allows you to go into instances where missions take place, and upon your return the hub will have changed. Other tribes may hear about your deeds as you progress and show up in the hub area.</li> <li>The player can see and make visits to the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Umbra\" target=\"_blank\">Umbra</a>, allowing communication and bartering with spirits. The trips however will be kept short.</li> <li>Will take place in natural environments but also typical industrial environments, such as a dam.</li> <li>Creatures that inhabit the World of Darkness will have a place in this game, for example Vampire: The Masquerade and Mage: The Ascension.</li> <li>Other tribes you encounter in the world may be hostile or friendly.</li> </ul><br /> <b>The Player Character</b><ul><li>The protagonist is a male Garou named Cahal of the Fianna tribe, who was banished years ago for reasons unknown. He became a <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Ronin_(WTA)\" target=\"_blank\">Ronin</a> and lost connection with his tribe's <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Totem\" target=\"_blank\">totem</a>. At the start of the game he returns to his old pack and the sacred <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Caern\" target=\"_blank\">Caern</a> they are protecting, following the massacre of his family and the disappearance of his son.</li> <li><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Fianna\" target=\"_blank\">Fianna</a> are celtic influenced werewolves, who value family very highly. Cahal's concept art also does feature celtic tattoos.</li> <li>Cahal can take on three forms at will: Lupus (wolf), Homid (human) and Crinos (werewolf).</li> <li>Glabro (near beast) and Hispo (dire wolf) forms are not going to be playable.</li> <li>They want it to be seamless to move between forms, for example making a long leap as a Lupus and shift into Crinos mid-jump.</li> <li>There are skill trees that lets you focus on a particular gameplay archetype with its own strength and weaknesses.</li> <li>There are mentions of Cahal's view on extremism among the Garou on the conflict, and how his matured world view would affect that, and the way his son changed while he was away.</li> </ul><b>Lupus (wolf)</b><br /><br /><ul><li>The travel form. Good for exploration, travel, stealth, sniffing out trails, and scouting foes. Can also enter areas that are otherwise too small to go through.</li> <li>Lupus form have access to Umbral vision that lets him see Wyrm influence on e.g. human guards.</li> </ul><b>Homid (human)</b><br /><br /><ul><li>The interaction form. Capable of silent takedowns of enemies, activating traps, drones, hacking and gathering information from computers, and of course talking with other humans. Humans are unable to distinguish werewolves so Cahal is able to easily move undercover in the Homid form.</li> <li>Wields a crossbow that can merge elemental spirits into it. Can be used to silently kill enemies, but also interact with the environment. For example exploding an explosive barrel with flaming arrows, or short circuit to open a door with an electrified arrow.</li> <li>Regenerates health while in Homid form. However if the player has taken damage from silver-based weapons, it'll stack an effect that gradually lower their max health.</li> <li>Homid form have access to Umbral vision that lets him see Wyrm influence on e.g. human guards.</li> </ul><b>Crinos (werewolf)</b><br /><br /><ul><li>The combat form. Savagely rip and tear your enemies as a werewolf. Build up Rage when you take damage, and reduce it by doing finishing moves. The higher the Rage, the more effective you'll be in combat by ways of unlocking stronger but slower attacks. But build up <i>too much</i> Rage, and you'll become Frenzied, which puts you into a state of uncontrollable rage.</li> <li>Is able to clear up a cluttered area and creating space for you to fight on.</li> <li>Rage can also build out of combat, by simple things like standing in a puddle of oil, seeing the corpse of an animal, a conversation about animal cruelty. This can then trigger a change to the Crinos form.</li> <li>It's possible for Cahal to become enraged even during dialogue, causing him to eviscerate an important character.</li> <li>You cannot leave Crinos form until all hostiles have been dealt with.</li> <li>When Frenzied, you can't tell friend from foe. Therefore to leave a frenzied Crinos form you need to kill <i>everything</i> and suffer the consequences. The frenzied Crinos form is more powerful but has more inertia and becomes more difficult to maneuver.</li> <li>When you are Frenzied you also attract the Wyrm, causing the Wyrm to spawn more enemies for you to fight in a sort of horde mode. It's intended to challenge those who enjoy combat, but at the same time you are on a timer. Too much time spent Frenzied fighting the Wyrm will eventually corrupt Cahal - resulting in a game over.</li> <li>Other characters and animals will feel your Rage if it gets high enough, and also have an effect on a player tattoo (OP: very little information on the player tattoo so far).</li> </ul><b>Enemies</b><br /><br /><ul><li>The main antagonistic faction is Endron Oil, which is closely affiliated with the Wyrm and owned by Pentex Industries. Pentex in turn is also owned by vampires.</li> <li>Endron Oil is aware of the existence of werewolves, and have guards using exoskeletons, silver weaponry and humans possessed by the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Fomori\" target=\"_blank\">Fomori</a> - a form of Wyrm spirit.</li> <li>Wyrm possessed humans will upon death release the Fomori spirit for you to fight.</li> <li>Cahal can detect the Wyrm presence in humans using Umbral vision.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T11:17:59-08:00","id":1187322,"title":"","content":"This sounds so fucking awesome.<br /> <br /> I'm actually getting a Marvel: Ultimate Alliance and X-Men Legends feel to the game; and that makes me so incredibly happy.<br /> <br /> <br /> There better be a collector's edition for this game...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T11:18:42-08:00","id":1187323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1187293#post1187293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>The <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Tribe_(WTA)\" target=\"_blank\">thirteen tribes of the Garou</a> are contemplating going into war with humanity due to their greed and destruction of the planet.</li> </ul><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This aspect really does not endear myself to it. I mean, I get that it is a very good concept, but war on humanity is silly when you got -human- kinfolk.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T17:33:28-08:00","id":1187402,"title":"","content":"Where's that from? I haven't seen anything that covers a lot of that explicitly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T18:28:48-08:00","id":1187420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1187323#post1187323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This aspect really does not endear myself to it. I mean, I get that it is a very good concept, but war on humanity is silly when you got -human- kinfolk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having the Umbra partly cut out also boggles the mind. It's supposed to be the world's soul; you have to dwell in spirit and flesh in order to safeguard both sides. This means regular visits, not rarely-used trips at the center of a handful of plot points. &quot;Rarely-visited&quot; is something that only makes sense in the context of Near-Realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T01:49:44-08:00","id":1187492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1187420#post1187420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Having the Umbra partly cut out also boggles the mind. It's supposed to be the world's soul; you have to dwell in spirit and flesh in order to safeguard both sides. This means regular visits, not rarely-used trips at the center of a handful of plot points. &quot;Rarely-visited&quot; is something that only makes sense in the context of Near-Realms.</div> </div> </div> </div>In-game, I'd say umbra might be hard to do as a frequent place to visit. I think if it is treated like the Fade in Dragon Age, I'd be content. Given there has not been a single released WtA game, gotta focus on getting this out at all before doing anything more complex.<br /> <br /> Personally, the gameplay seems good (as a concept) and I do not want this to fail. The lore just baffles me, given more and more the BNS book's promise seems to be accurate.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T03:39:29-08:00","id":1187507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1187323#post1187323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This aspect really does not endear myself to it. I mean, I get that it is a very good concept, but war on humanity is silly when you got -human- kinfolk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there is the humanity and there is the family, us and them.<br /> We against the world,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T07:25:57-08:00","id":1187546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1187492#post1187492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The lore just baffles me, given more and more the BNS book's promise seems to be accurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T08:20:37-08:00","id":1187560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1187492#post1187492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In-game, I'd say umbra might be hard to do as a frequent place to visit. I think if it is treated like the Fade in Dragon Age, I'd be content. Given there has not been a single released WtA game, gotta focus on getting this out at all before doing anything more complex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is this complex? Use the Soul Reaver Spectral Realm method from way back in 1999 and you can easily at least handle the Penumbra.<br /> <br /> I get why this stuff was a hurdle back with Heart of Gaia... but other games have thoroughly shown this can be done if you want to do it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T08:36:00-08:00","id":1187562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1187507#post1187507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well there is the humanity and there is the family, us and them.<br /> We against the world,</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but you never know who is kin, besides most garou grow up in human society and so much of their culture can be tied to their people. Red Talons can rarr about Impegrium because they don't have ties to humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1187546#post1187546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What do you mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Things from the BNS MET book have popped up in Changing Ways, from the limited gauntlet to the male Fury metis (which was fixed in the final edition, luckily). Generally, what is in that MET book, is most likely going to be the new canon for WtA.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1187560#post1187560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why is this complex? Use the Soul Reaver Spectral Realm method from way back in 1999 and you can easily at least handle the Penumbra.<br /> <br /> I get why this stuff was a hurdle back with Heart of Gaia... but other games have thoroughly shown this can be done if you want to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on what sort of engine they are using and the skills of their programmers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 02-19-2018, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T12:03:32-08:00","id":1187611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1187562#post1187562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Things from the BNS MET book have popped up in Changing Ways, from the limited gauntlet to the male Fury metis (which was fixed in the final edition, luckily). Generally, what is in that MET book, is most likely going to be the new canon for WtA.</div> </div> </div> </div>Random question: by the &quot;MET book&quot; do you mean the old playtest slices, or the actual final MET book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T16:06:46-08:00","id":1187675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1187611#post1187611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Random question: by the &quot;MET book&quot; do you mean the old playtest slices, or the actual final MET book?</div> </div> </div> </div>The final MET book, I bought it to go over it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T07:24:06-08:00","id":1187830,"title":"","content":"They mentioned that umbral quests will not be too long<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T10:20:48-08:00","id":1187887,"title":"","content":"A fetish crossbow is nice and all but, since we're a Fianna, could we have a Threefold Axe instead?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T12:08:32-08:00","id":1187932,"title":"","content":"A klaive would still make me happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T22:45:54-08:00","id":1194141,"title":"","content":"I'm so disappointed that they are going with a pre-defined protagonist with a set tribe. If you didn't want to put the work in for all thirteen tribes, fine, go with a Ronin, but why set the character then? Let us choose aspect, gender, former tribe, origin, etc. etc. <br /> <br /> I mean, this is based on a RPG. Where the point is making your own character. It's not like having multiple origins, especially if you have them all end in being a Ronin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/480-blind-dragon","name":"Blind Dragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T06:13:36-07:00","id":1194503,"title":"","content":"It is really very disappointing that you cannot choose the tribe your character will be part of.<br /> A Werewolf the Apocalypse equivalent to Vampire the Masquerade: Bloodlines would be incredible, and that is how I first imagined the game when they announced it.<br /> <br /> Doesn't mean I won't be playing it, I'll just not enjoy it as much as I thought I would.<br /> But then again, this is a pretty early announcement, isn't it? Games tend to change a lot from the first announcement of features to the final version. Hopefully, it'll be what we want it to be and what a WtA game deserves to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23978-tatacavalier","name":"TataCavalier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T09:34:23-07:00","id":1199735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1187293#post1187293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>The <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Tribe_(WTA)&quot;]thirteen</a> tribes of the Garou[/URL] are contemplating going into war with humanity due to their greed and destruction of the planet.</li> <li>You do not choose your tribe at the start of the game.</li> <li>You do not control a party of characters, you are solitary. You have allies outside of combat however.</li> <li>Takes place in Nevada, Alaska and the redwood forests of Washington.</li> <li>You do not align yourself to tribes as you play through the game, but you will encounter them and learn about their perspective of the conflict with humanity and the Wyrm.</li> <li>Levels are semi-open and linear, but offers multiple ways to solve it similar to Deus Ex.</li> <li>Each region have a large hub with free-roaming environment and different activities to do. Aid spirits of nature, such as destroying a dam to earn the favor of a river spirit, or destroy outposts. One such favor to a spirit can for example open a shortcut between regions or grant more side-missions. The hub allows you to go into instances where missions take place, and upon your return the hub will have changed. Other tribes may hear about your deeds as you progress and show up in the hub area.</li> <li>The player can see and make visits to the <a href=\"http://&quot;http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Umbra&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Umbra</a>, allowing communication and bartering with spirits. The trips however will be kept short.</li> <li>Will take place in natural environments but also typical industrial environments, such as a dam.</li> <li>Creatures that inhabit the World of Darkness will have a place in this game, for example Vampire: The Masquerade and Mage: The Ascension.</li> <li>Other tribes you encounter in the world may be hostile or friendly.</li> </ul><b>The Player Character</b><ul><li>The protagonist is a male Garou named Cahal of the Fianna tribe, who was banished years ago for reasons unknown. He became a <a href=\"http://&quot;http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Ronin_(WTA)&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Ronin</a> and lost connection with his tribe's <a href=\"http://&quot;http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Totem&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">totem</a>. At the start of the game he returns to his old pack and the sacred <a href=\"http://&quot;http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Caern&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Caern</a> they are protecting, following the massacre of his family and the disappearance of his son.</li> <li><a href=\"http://&quot;http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Fianna&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Fianna</a> are celtic influenced werewolves, who value family very highly. Cahal's concept art also does feature celtic tattoos.</li> <li>Cahal can take on three forms at will: Lupus (wolf), Homid (human) and Crinos (werewolf).</li> <li>Glabro (near beast) and Hispo (dire wolf) forms are not going to be playable.</li> <li>They want it to be seamless to move between forms, for example making a long leap as a Lupus and shift into Crinos mid-jump.</li> <li>There are skill trees that lets you focus on a particular gameplay archetype with its own strength and weaknesses.</li> <li>There are mentions of Cahal's view on extremism among the Garou on the conflict, and how his matured world view would affect that, and the way his son changed while he was away.</li> </ul><b>Lupus (wolf)</b><ul><li>The travel form. Good for exploration, travel, stealth, sniffing out trails, and scouting foes. Can also enter areas that are otherwise too small to go through.</li> <li>Lupus form have access to Umbral vision that lets him see Wyrm influence on e.g. human guards.</li> </ul><b>Homid (human)</b><ul><li>The interaction form. Capable of silent takedowns of enemies, activating traps, drones, hacking and gathering information from computers, and of course talking with other humans. Humans are unable to distinguish werewolves so Cahal is able to easily move undercover in the Homid form.</li> <li>Wields a crossbow that can merge elemental spirits into it. Can be used to silently kill enemies, but also interact with the environment. For example exploding an explosive barrel with flaming arrows, or short circuit to open a door with an electrified arrow.</li> <li>Regenerates health while in Homid form. However if the player has taken damage from silver-based weapons, it'll stack an effect that gradually lower their max health.</li> <li>Homid form have access to Umbral vision that lets him see Wyrm influence on e.g. human guards.</li> </ul><b>Crinos (werewolf)</b><ul><li>The combat form. Savagely rip and tear your enemies as a werewolf. Build up Rage when you take damage, and reduce it by doing finishing moves. The higher the Rage, the more effective you'll be in combat by ways of unlocking stronger but slower attacks. But build up <i>too much</i> Rage, and you'll become Frenzied, which puts you into a state of uncontrollable rage.</li> <li>Is able to clear up a cluttered area and creating space for you to fight on.</li> <li>Rage can also build out of combat, by simple things like standing in a puddle of oil, seeing the corpse of an animal, a conversation about animal cruelty. This can then trigger a change to the Crinos form.</li> <li>It's possible for Cahal to become enraged even during dialogue, causing him to eviscerate an important character.</li> <li>You cannot leave Crinos form until all hostiles have been dealt with.</li> <li>When Frenzied, you can't tell friend from foe. Therefore to leave a frenzied Crinos form you need to kill <i>everything</i> and suffer the consequences. The frenzied Crinos form is more powerful but has more inertia and becomes more difficult to maneuver.</li> <li>When you are Frenzied you also attract the Wyrm, causing the Wyrm to spawn more enemies for you to fight in a sort of horde mode. It's intended to challenge those who enjoy combat, but at the same time you are on a timer. Too much time spent Frenzied fighting the Wyrm will eventually corrupt Cahal - resulting in a game over.</li> <li>Other characters and animals will feel your Rage if it gets high enough, and also have an effect on a player tattoo (OP: very little information on the player tattoo so far).</li> </ul><b>Enemies</b><ul><li>The main antagonistic faction is Endron Oil, which is closely affiliated with the Wyrm and owned by Pentex Industries. Pentex in turn is also owned by vampires.</li> <li>Endron Oil is aware of the existence of werewolves, and have guards using exoskeletons, silver weaponry and humans possessed by the <a href=\"http://&quot;http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Fomori&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Fomori</a> - a form of Wyrm spirit.</li> <li>Wyrm possessed humans will upon death release the Fomori spirit for you to fight.</li> <li>Cahal can detect the Wyrm presence in humans using Umbral vision.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>The game takes place in Alaska, the main enemy is drilling firm and the protagonist is a lone warrior. His name should be Steven <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> But seriously, great job finding these info. I see you are as restless as I am in my quest for Heart of Gaia working prototype <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. And I'm still searching Weaver's Web song from this game. <br /> <br /> For those who oppose playing a pregen: Cahal WAS Fianna. But in the beginning he is a Ronin. Thing that bothers me more is which rank he achieved before his exile, cause Ronins may lost their status but not their skills and powers.<br /> <br /> As for creating character: according to the main rulebook the character which can join the biggest number of tribes is female lupus with very few backgrounds (and Pure Breed determine which tribes will be unavailable, Silver Fangs or Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers). Not my favourite type of character. Of course as a ST I'm more versatile than the paper.<br /> <br /> And one question: what kind of NPCs/which characters would you like to see in this game? I would love to meet some of characters from previous WoD-based video games as some kind of easter eggs (my favourites are Julia Anderson from Mage the Ascension Refugee, father Esteban Cortes from Hunter: The Reckoning series and of course Ryan Dances-the-Spiral McCullough). As for NPCs Malkavian with somatoparaphrenia would be great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 03-26-2018, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T07:17:36-07:00","id":1200024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1199735#post1199735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And one question: what kind of NPCs/which characters would you like to see in this game? I would love to meet some of characters from previous WoD-based video games as some kind of easter eggs (my favourites are Julia Anderson from Mage the Ascension Refugee, father Esteban Cortes from Hunter: The Reckoning series and of course Ryan Dances-the-Spiral McCullough). As for NPCs Malkavian with somatoparaphrenia would be great.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for your brotherly words, we are many, we are one aroooo.....<br /> Ahem, apart from that we will all kinds of monsters, mages, fomori, banes vampires, etcetc, also there are rumours about Red Talons and Glass Walkers.<br /> Also, man if anyone out there manages to stick together a heart of Gaia prototype, we have to crown him emperor of mankind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 03-27-2018, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T08:21:58-07:00","id":1200040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1200024#post1200024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for your brotherly words, we are many, we are one aroooo.....<br /> Ahem, apart from that we will all kinds of monsters, mages, fomori, banes vampires, etcetc, also there are rumours about Red Talons and Glass Walkers.<br /> Also, man if anyone out there manages to stick together a heart of Gaia prototype, we have to crown him emperor of mankind.</div> </div> </div> </div>But, as Cahal will be male homid it will be difficult for him to join Red Talons or Black Furies.<br /> <br /> And why mankind. I think it should be rather Silver Crown for him <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T12:43:41-07:00","id":1200189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1200040#post1200040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But, as Cahal will be male homid it will be difficult for him to join Red Talons or Black Furies.<br /> <br /> And why mankind. I think it should be rather Silver Crown for him <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm Cahala the Silver Queen, not a bad idea at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T12:54:39-07:00","id":1200192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1181902-guess-what-new-werewolf-ta-computer-game-announced?p=1200189#post1200189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hmm Cahala the Silver Queen, not a bad idea at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant Silver Crown for anyone who will get us fully functional Heart of Gaia prototype.<br /> <br /> Hmmm, the main character becomes more interesting. According to the SSN census there isn't any Cahal registered in USA (or this name has less than 5 occurrences a year). Wonder if the creators of Earth Blood know that. This name meaning is powerful in battle or ready for war BTW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 03-27-2018, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T12:15:58-07:00","id":1200515,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13141\" data-vbnamecard=\"13141\">Nail Eater</a> from what I've heard yes they do lots of research, they want this game to be good.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T19:04:35-07:00","id":1201797,"title":"","content":"Another interesting fact about main character's name: its other form is Cathal. Cathal was also the name of first king of house Balor. Their Royal Guards protect their greatest treasures, among which is Balor Crystal Eye, taken from Balor the Evil Eye by one of the Fomorians. Eye of Balor is also a changeling's term for the Red Star aka Anthelios <img src=